<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Woodside to plug Spica-1 oil well.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Woodside to plug Spica-1 oil well.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodside Petroleum Ltd said on Monday it will plug and abandon the Spica-1 exploration well in the Dampier sub-basin of the North West Shelf off Western Australia.</p>
<p>Preliminary observations of core samples and logs indicates there are no significant hydrocarbons present, it said.</p>
<p>The well is contained in the WA-4-L exploration license held one-sixth each by Woodside, Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd, British Petroleum Co Plc, Chevron Inc Royal/Dutch Shell and Japan (LNG) MiMi Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
